# - resource -------------------------------------------------------------------

<http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL2BPMNClasses> a fhir:CodeSystem ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "KGL2BPMNClasses"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><div xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\"><hr/><p><b>English</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem KGL2BPMNClasses</b></p><a name=\"KGL2BPMNClasses\"> </a><a name=\"hcKGL2BPMNClasses\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL2BPMNClasses</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-definitions<a name=\"KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-definitions\"> </a></td><td>BPMN File</td><td>One BPMN file as a unit -- the `bpmn:definitions` root. Shares its IRI with the l1:external-artifact for the same file, so the component that points at it and the subgraph that opens it name one resource.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-process<a name=\"KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-process\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Process</td><td>One `bpmn:process`. Present as a node because a participant references it by processRef, and without it the pool-to-element attribution has nothing to travel through.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-participant<a name=\"KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-participant\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Participant</td><td>A pool: a role that owns part of the collaboration. The lifecycle BPMN has 8 and declares no laneSet at all, so the pool is the only unit of role assignment present and its @name is the sole link to a persona.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-task<a name=\"KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-task\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Task</td><td>A task or sub-process. It is what a DMN usingTask href points at, what sequence flows connect, and what a DAK-level task entry describes. Sub-processes carry isSubProcess rather than getting a class of their own -- the lifecycle BPMN has exactly one.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-gateway<a name=\"KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-gateway\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Gateway</td><td>A branch or merge. Included for connectivity rather than for a cross-model edge: a flow through a gateway with no node would point at nothing, and every reachability question over the process would break at the first decision point.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-event<a name=\"KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-event\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Event</td><td>A start, end or intermediate event (WHO's DAK BPMN draw intermediate throw and catch events inside sub-processes). Same connectivity argument as gateway, plus one of its own: entry and exit points are what make 'is this task reachable' and 'does this path terminate' answerable at all.</td></tr></table></div><div xml:lang=\"fr\" lang=\"fr\"><hr/><p><b>French</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Narratif généré : CodeSystem KGL2BPMNClasses</b></p><a name=\"fr-KGL2BPMNClasses\"> </a><a name=\"fr-hcKGL2BPMNClasses\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL2BPMNClasses</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Affichage</b></td><td><b>Définition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-definitions<a name=\"fr-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-definitions\"> </a></td><td>BPMN File</td><td>One BPMN file as a unit -- the `bpmn:definitions` root. Shares its IRI with the l1:external-artifact for the same file, so the component that points at it and the subgraph that opens it name one resource.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-process<a name=\"fr-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-process\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Process</td><td>One `bpmn:process`. Present as a node because a participant references it by processRef, and without it the pool-to-element attribution has nothing to travel through.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-participant<a name=\"fr-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-participant\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Participant</td><td>A pool: a role that owns part of the collaboration. The lifecycle BPMN has 8 and declares no laneSet at all, so the pool is the only unit of role assignment present and its @name is the sole link to a persona.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-task<a name=\"fr-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-task\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Task</td><td>A task or sub-process. It is what a DMN usingTask href points at, what sequence flows connect, and what a DAK-level task entry describes. Sub-processes carry isSubProcess rather than getting a class of their own -- the lifecycle BPMN has exactly one.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-gateway<a name=\"fr-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-gateway\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Gateway</td><td>A branch or merge. Included for connectivity rather than for a cross-model edge: a flow through a gateway with no node would point at nothing, and every reachability question over the process would break at the first decision point.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-event<a name=\"fr-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-event\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Event</td><td>A start, end or intermediate event (WHO's DAK BPMN draw intermediate throw and catch events inside sub-processes). Same connectivity argument as gateway, plus one of its own: entry and exit points are what make 'is this task reachable' and 'does this path terminate' answerable at all.</td></tr></table></div><div xml:lang=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\"><hr/><p><b>Arabic</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>السرد المُنشأ: CodeSystem KGL2BPMNClasses</b></p><a name=\"ar-KGL2BPMNClasses\"> </a><a name=\"ar-hcKGL2BPMNClasses\"> </a><p>يُعرّف هذا case-sensitive نظام الشيفرة <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL2BPMNClasses</code> الرمز التالي<f test=\"code-count != 1\">s</f>:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>الكود</b></td><td><b>العرض</b></td><td><b>التعريف</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-definitions<a name=\"ar-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-definitions\"> </a