 reachable' and 'does this path terminate' answerable at all.</td></tr></table></div><div xml:lang=\"zh\" lang=\"zh\"><hr/><p><b>Chinese</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: 代码系统 KGL2BPMNClasses</b></p><a name=\"zh-KGL2BPMNClasses\"> </a><a name=\"zh-hcKGL2BPMNClasses\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL2BPMNClasses</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-definitions<a name=\"zh-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-definitions\"> </a></td><td>BPMN File</td><td>One BPMN file as a unit -- the `bpmn:definitions` root. Shares its IRI with the l1:external-artifact for the same file, so the component that points at it and the subgraph that opens it name one resource.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-process<a name=\"zh-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-process\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Process</td><td>One `bpmn:process`. Present as a node because a participant references it by processRef, and without it the pool-to-element attribution has nothing to travel through.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-participant<a name=\"zh-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-participant\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Participant</td><td>A pool: a role that owns part of the collaboration. The lifecycle BPMN has 8 and declares no laneSet at all, so the pool is the only unit of role assignment present and its @name is the sole link to a persona.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-task<a name=\"zh-KGL2BPMNClasses-bpmn-task\"> </a></td><td>BPMN Task</td><td>A task or sub-process. It is what a DMN usingTask href points at, what sequence flows connect, and what a DAK-level task entry describes. Sub-processes carry isSubProcess rather than getting a class of their own -- the lifecycle BPMN has exactly one.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bpmn-gate